# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props type: `ComponentNameProps` — define with `type`, e.g. `type ComponentNameProps = { ... }`
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for simple types
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## How to verify

- `yarn test:typecheck` — confirms strict TypeScript and imports for edited packages.
- `yarn test:code` and `yarn test:other` — ESLint and Prettier match repo style.
- Run or add colocated `*.test.tsx` / `*.test.ts` and execute via `yarn test:app` (see `.cursor/rules/testing.mdc` for the full script list).
